# Copy to .env and fill in the values before `docker compose up`.

# Required: the vault's folder on the Docker host, mounted as /vault.
VAULT_HOST_PATH=
# Required: the server's URL as the app reaches it (https://...), for
# pairing links. The server refuses to start without it.
PUBLIC_URL=
# The host address the server's port is published on (docker-compose.yml).
# Default 127.0.0.1: only a reverse proxy on the same host reaches it. Set
# the LAN or Tailscale address the proxy uses instead; never 0.0.0.0 on a
# host with a public address.
# BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1
# Behind a reverse proxy: Express "trust proxy", so the /pair rate limit
# sees client IPs. Best: the proxy's exact IP (or CIDR). Also valid:
# loopback, uniquelocal, a hop count such as 1. Not "true" (startup fails).
# uniquelocal trusts X-Forwarded-For from any private address, so a LAN
# client reaching :3099 directly can dodge the limit.
# TRUST_PROXY=
# Optional: a shared token, for typing the address and a token into the
# app by hand instead of pairing. While set, it works next to the device
# tokens; remove it to allow paired devices only.
# AUTH_TOKEN=
# Only for a browser client: its origin, e.g. http://localhost:8081.
# Unset: no CORS headers; the iOS app needs none.
# CORS_ORIGIN=
# A public demo server only, never your own: a pairing code any device may
# use, again and again, until the expiry (an ISO date: 2026-12-15 or
# 2026-12-15T12:00:00Z). Off unless both are set; set but invalid stops the
# server. The code: at least 16 random bytes, base64url, e.g.
# `openssl rand 24 | basenc --base64url`. Its link: scripts/demo-pair-link.sh.
# At most DEMO_MAX_DEVICES (default 20) demo devices; a new pairing past
# that revokes the oldest.
# DEMO_PAIRING_CODE=
# DEMO_PAIRING_EXPIRES=
# DEMO_MAX_DEVICES=20
